{
  "_snapshot": "AS BUILT + REAL-PAYLOAD CORRECTED 2026-08-14 — live in n8n as 'Sales — Booking Recovery Capture (iClosed)' (31DnMJLU3YM89py1), published, writing to Data Table booking_recovery (xEhLpKwNv8uTaeAK). This file is a reference copy; the live version is authoritative and its field mappings are now CONFIRMED against real deliveries (executions 382967/382968), not inferred from docs. Four things the real payload disproved: (1) iClosed can emit TWO contact records for ONE human on a single form fill — a new one plus an existing one matched by phone — so lead_key is phone-first, not iClosed-contact-id, or that person gets emailed twice; (2) the calendar slug lives at event.linkPrefix ('synchrosocial/<slug>'), not eventSlug, and capture is now GATED to acquisition calendars so a client booking their onboarding kickoff is never chased; (3) the Meta click id arrives as tracking._fbc ('fb.1.<ts>.<fbclid>'), never as fbclid, and the referrer as body.Referrer_Url_Embed; (4) questionsAndAnswers carries the whole qualification form — revenue, timeline, decision-maker — which is the most valuable thing in the payload and is now stored. Also: primary email can be blank while the value just typed lands in secondary_email. Verified by replays 382974 (new lead armed, phone key, fbclid extracted), 382975 (second iClosed record for the same human routed to touch and enriched row 5 rather than creating a duplicate) and 382976 (kickoff-call suppressed as other_calendar).",
